From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: VIctory contributor <contributor@users.noreply.invalid>
Date: Wed, 25 Nov 2026 03:05:09 -0500
Subject: [PATCH 31/43] Series S: the title keeps its own upscaler, not FSR 4
 (its frames were black)

The title chooses its upscaler by console: on a Series S with the
FidelityFX capability, FSR 4 (type 7); otherwise its own (type 6, as on a
Series X). FSR 4's output never reaches the screen under VIctory, so every
world frame was black with `--console series-s`, and holding its DLL back
makes the title divide by zero in the FSR 4 wrapper.

The known build now carries code patches (victory-game: per-build RVA, a
short signature checked before anything is written, our own bytes): both
functions that make the choice return 6. The prepared copy is patched
before it is mapped and gets a file name of its own.
VICTORY_TITLE_PATCHES=0 turns them off; VICTORY_TITLE_PATCH=<rva>:<old>:<new>
adds more.

In game (RTX 3090 Ti, Series S, no switches): the prologue renders, 6.1 to
6.4 fps steady (about 73 ms on the GPU), against 4.7 to 4.8 fps on the
Series X profile.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
(cherry picked from commit c750c57f04274fe43fe2dd8be2c0d83e27e85cfb)
